cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. The dataset built with it has its own citation; see README.md."
type: software
title: "LocalNet-Dynamics: collector, build pipeline and analysis toolkit for longitudinal home-network telemetry"
authors:
  - family-names: "Ezharjan"
    given-names: "Alexander"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-09"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/Ezharjan/LocalNetDynamicsDataset"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ezharjan/LocalNetDynamicsDataset"
abstract: >-
  A Python toolkit that samples a local network every 30 seconds from a client
  machine (ICMP latency, jitter and loss to a reference host and to the
  gateway, TCP connect time, cached and recursive DNS response time, HTTP
  time-to-first-response, Wi-Fi link metrics and periodic WAN/LAN throughput
  tests), consolidates the raw runs into a labelled dataset, and produces the
  statistics and figures that document it.
keywords:
  - network telemetry
  - network measurement
  - latency
  - jitter
  - packet loss
  - DNS
  - throughput
  - quality of service
  - anomaly detection
  - time series
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "LocalNet-Dynamics: A Longitudinal Local Area Network Telemetry Dataset"
